Package: kubeos-storage
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, lvm2, xfsprogs, python3
Description: KubeOS dynamic local storage: the pod-data volume and its provisioner
 First boot takes the free space the installer deliberately leaves inside kubeos-vg,
 creates a thin pool, formats the pod-data volume with XFS and mounts it at
 /opt/local-path-provisioner, so workload data never fills /. kubeos-storage-provisioner
 then serves the default "local-path" StorageClass from that volume as a plain systemd
 service - no helper Pod per volume, which is the whole reason it replaced upstream's
 design on an appliance that runs no Pods in its base system.
 .
 Both operations are idempotent and never destroy data: the pool is only created when it
 does not exist, and a formatted volume is never re-formatted.
